---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = "Nutrition & Healthy Eating | Marietta Childcare";
const description = "Comprehensive guide to meal planning, nutrition information, allergy management, and healthy snacks for growing children.";
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <section class="relative py-32 overflow-hidden w-screen -ml-[calc((100vw-100%)/2)]">
    <div class="absolute inset-0 z-0">
      <img 
        src="/images/Background_Images/group_snack_time_healthy_eating_background.jpg" 
        alt="Nutrition guide" 
        class="w-full h-full object-cover"
      />
      <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-black/40"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="relative z-10 max-w-[1280px] mx-auto px-6 lg:px-20">
      <h1 class="text-4xl lg:text-6xl font-black mb-6 text-white drop-shadow-lg">Nutrition & Healthy Eating Guide</h1>
      <p class="text-lg mb-12 max-w-2xl text-white drop-shadow-md">Comprehensive nutrition guidance for parents seeking to support their child's healthy growth and development.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="min-h-screen">
    <!-- Hero Section -->
    <section class="bg-gradient-to-r from-orange-50 to-amber-50 py-12 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Nutrition & Healthy Eating: Supporting Child Growth and Development</h1>
        <p class="text-xl text-gray-700 mb-6">
          Marietta Childcare prioritizes Child Nutrition as a foundation for healthy development. Child Nutrition supports physical growth, cognitive development, and energy levels necessary for active learning. Marietta Childcare's Nutrition Program provides balanced meals and snacks that meet children's developmental nutritional needs.
        </p>
        <a href="/contact" class="inline-block bg-orange-600 text-white px-6 py-3 rounded-lg font-semibold hover:bg-orange-700">Learn About Our Meals</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Content Section -->
    <section class="py-12 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        
        <!-- Nutritional Needs by Age -->
        <div class="mb-12">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6">Nutritional Needs by Age Group</h2>
          
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            Nutritional Requirements vary significantly across childhood ages. Nutritional Needs reflect each child's growth rate, activity level, and developmental stage. Marietta Childcare's meal planning ensures that Nutritional Requirements are met for each age group served in our programs.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4">Infant Nutrition: Birth to 12 Months</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            Infant Nutrition begins with breast milk or formula as the primary nutrition source. Infant Nutrition during the first 6 months is exclusively breast milk or formula, which provides all necessary nutrients. Infant Nutrition transitions around 6 months with introduction of solid foods—iron-fortified cereals, pureed vegetables, and pureed fruits. Infant Nutrition at 8-12 months includes soft finger foods, allowing infants to practice self-feeding skills while continuing breast milk or formula as the primary nutrition source.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4">Toddler Nutrition: 12 to 36 Months</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            Toddler Nutrition emphasizes variety and self-feeding development. Toddler Nutrition includes foods from all food groups—proteins, grains, fruits, vegetables, and dairy—in age-appropriate portions. Toddler Nutrition supports rapid growth and brain development, requiring adequate protein, healthy fats, and micronutrients like iron, zinc, and calcium. Toddler Nutrition meals at Marietta Childcare are designed to be finger-food friendly, supporting toddlers' developing independence while ensuring adequate nutrition.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4">Preschool Nutrition: Ages 3 to 5</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            Preschool Nutrition continues to emphasize balanced meals with foods from all food groups. Preschool Nutrition supports continued growth and provides energy for active play and learning. Preschool Nutrition includes teaching children about healthy food choices and involving them in meal preparation activities. Preschool Nutrition at Marietta Childcare models healthy eating habits and creates positive associations with nutritious foods.
          </p>

          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-6">
            Marietta Childcare's Nutrition Program is designed by professionals familiar with Child Nutrition requirements at each developmental stage, ensuring that all children receive appropriate nutrition for their age and developmental needs.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Meal Planning -->
        <div class="mb-12">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6">Meal Planning and Food Variety</h2>
          
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            Meal Planning at Marietta Childcare follows nutritional guidelines and incorporates food variety. Meal Planning ensures that children experience diverse foods, developing broader palates and exposure to different nutrients. Meal Planning includes seasonal foods, cultural diversity, and consideration of children's developing taste preferences.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4">Balanced Meal Components</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            Balanced Meals include protein, whole grains, fruits, vegetables, and dairy. Balanced Meals provide sustained energy, support growth, and develop healthy eating patterns. Balanced Meals at Marietta Childcare feature colorful vegetables, whole grain breads and cereals, lean proteins, and calcium-rich dairy products. Balanced Meals are prepared fresh whenever possible, avoiding processed foods high in sodium and added sugars.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4">Introducing New Foods</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            Food Introduction follows developmental guidelines and respects individual readiness. Food Introduction for infants begins with single-ingredient foods, allowing parents and educators to identify potential allergies. Food Introduction for older children includes exposure to new foods in low-pressure environments. Food Introduction is most successful when new foods are offered multiple times—research shows children often need 10-15 exposures to accept new foods.
          </p>

          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-6">
            Marietta Childcare's Meal Planning creates positive Food Experiences that support children's developing independence and healthy eating habits throughout life.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Allergy Management -->
        <div class="mb-12">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6">Allergy Management and Food Safety</h2>
          
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            Food Allergies affect many children and require careful management. Food Allergy Management at Marietta Childcare includes detailed documentation of each child's allergies, careful meal planning to avoid allergens, and staff training on allergy protocols. Food Allergy Management ensures that children with allergies can participate safely in all meals and snacks.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4">Common Childhood Allergies</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            Common Allergens in childhood include peanuts, tree nuts, milk, eggs, wheat, soy, fish, and shellfish. Common Allergens account for the majority of childhood food allergies. Common Allergen Management requires reading food labels carefully, communicating with families about ingredients, and maintaining separate food preparation areas when necessary. Marietta Childcare takes Food Allergies seriously and maintains strict protocols to prevent cross-contamination.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4">Emergency Preparedness for Severe Allergies</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            Severe Food Allergies require emergency preparedness. Severe Allergy Management includes having emergency medications like epinephrine auto-injectors readily available, training staff on administration, and maintaining clear communication with families. Severe Allergy Protocols are reviewed regularly and practiced to ensure staff readiness. Marietta Childcare's commitment to Food Safety includes comprehensive Allergy Management protocols that protect children with severe allergies.
          </p>

          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-6">
            Parents of children with Food Allergies can trust that Marietta Childcare takes their child's safety seriously and maintains vigilant Allergy Management practices.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Healthy Snacks -->
        <div class="mb-12">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6">Healthy Snacks and Nutrition Education</h2>
          
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            Healthy Snacks provide important nutrition between meals and support sustained energy for learning and play. Healthy Snacks at Marietta Childcare feature whole grains, fruits, vegetables, proteins, and dairy rather than processed foods high in sugar and sodium. Healthy Snacks are planned to complement meals and provide variety in food experiences.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4">Snack Ideas for Home</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            Healthy Snack Options at home might include fresh fruit, yogurt, cheese, whole grain crackers, nuts or seeds, vegetables with hummus, or whole grain toast with nut butter. Healthy Snacks should be offered at consistent times to support healthy appetite regulation. Healthy Snacks avoid sugary drinks and processed snack foods that provide empty calories without nutritional benefit.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4">Teaching Children About Nutrition</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            Nutrition Education begins in early childhood through hands-on experiences. Nutrition Education includes involving children in meal preparation, growing vegetables in gardens, visiting farmers markets, and discussing food groups. Nutrition Education helps children develop awareness of how food supports their bodies and energy levels. Nutrition Education at Marietta Childcare creates positive associations with healthy foods and builds foundation for lifelong healthy eating habits.
          </p>

          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-6">
            Marietta Childcare integrates Nutrition Education throughout daily routines, helping children develop understanding and appreciation for nutritious foods.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Nutrition and Development -->
        <div class="mb-12">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6">Nutrition's Role in Child Development</h2>
          
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            Nutrition directly impacts Child Development across all domains. Nutrition supports Physical Development through provision of building blocks for growth. Nutrition supports Cognitive Development through adequate protein, healthy fats, and micronutrients essential for brain function. Nutrition supports Social-Emotional Development by ensuring children have energy and stable blood sugar for emotional regulation.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4">Brain Development and Nutrition</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            Brain Development requires specific nutrients, particularly during early childhood when brain growth is most rapid. Brain Development is supported by adequate protein, healthy fats (especially omega-3 fatty acids), iron, zinc, and B vitamins. Brain Development is compromised by inadequate nutrition, which can impact cognitive function, attention, and learning capacity. Marietta Childcare's Nutrition Program prioritizes nutrients essential for Brain Development.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4">Nutrition and Behavior</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            Nutrition significantly impacts Behavior and Emotional Regulation. Adequate Nutrition supports stable blood sugar, which enables better Emotional Regulation and behavior control. Inadequate Nutrition or excessive sugar consumption can contribute to hyperactivity, difficulty concentrating, and emotional dysregulation. Nutrition that includes protein and healthy fats provides sustained energy and supports Behavior stability throughout the day.
          </p>

          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-6">
            Marietta Childcare recognizes that Nutrition is foundational to Child Development and creates Nutrition Programs that support optimal development across all domains.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- CTA Section -->
        <div class="bg-orange-50 rounded-lg p-8 mb-12">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Experience Marietta Childcare's Nutrition Program</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-700 mb-6">
            Marietta Childcare's commitment to Child Nutrition ensures that every child receives meals and snacks that support their growth, development, and learning. Our Nutrition Program reflects best practices in child nutrition and developmental science.
          </p>
          <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4">
            <a href="/contact" class="inline-block bg-orange-600 text-white px-6 py-3 rounded-lg font-semibold hover:bg-orange-700">Schedule a Tour</a>
            <a href="/programs" class="inline-block bg-white text-orange-600 px-6 py-3 rounded-lg font-semibold border-2 border-orange-600 hover:bg-orange-50">View Our Programs</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Related Resources -->
        <div class="mb-12">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6">Related Nutrition Resources</h2>
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
            <div class="border border-gray-200 rounded-lg p-6">
              <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-3">
                <a href="/resources/child-development" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">Child Development Guide</a>
              </h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700">Understand how nutrition supports developmental milestones and growth across all developmental domains.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="border border-gray-200 rounded-lg p-6">
              <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-3">
                <a href="/resources/parenting-tips" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">Parenting Tips & Advice</a>
              </h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700">Get strategies for supporting your child's health, wellness, and development at home.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="border border-gray-200 rounded-lg p-6">
              <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-3">
                <a href="/programs/infant-care" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">Infant Care Program</a>
              </h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700">Learn about our specialized nutrition and feeding practices for infants from birth to 12 months.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="border border-gray-200 rounded-lg p-6">
              <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-3">
                <a href="/faq/nutrition-meals" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">Meals and Snacks FAQ</a>
              </h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700">Find answers to common questions about our meal planning, snacks, and allergy accommodations.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Schema Markup -->
    <script type="application/ld+json">
    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "Article",
      "headline": "Nutrition & Healthy Eating: Supporting Child Growth and Development",
      "description": "Comprehensive guide to meal planning, nutrition information, allergy management, and healthy snacks for growing children",
      "author": {
        "@type": "Organization",
        "name": "Marietta Childcare"
      },
      "publisher": {
        "@type": "Organization",
        "name": "Marietta Childcare",
        "logo": {
          "@type": "ImageObject",
          "url": "https://mariettachildcare.com/logo.png"
        }
      },
      "datePublished": "2024-01-01",
      "dateModified": "2024-01-01"
    }
    </script>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
